<title>LEBANON: Lebanon's foreign debt falls $10 million in Oct.</title>
<headline>Lebanon's foreign debt falls $10 million in Oct.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's foreign debt fell $10 million in October to $1,636 million from $1,646 million in September, the finance ministry said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Foreign debt was $1,312.6 million in December 1995.</p>
<p>Net Domestic Debt rose 309 billion Lebanese pounds to 12,743 billion from 12,434 billion in September, the ministry said.</p>
<p>The total outstanding debt in October was $9,826 million compared with $9,624 million in September, it added.</p>
<p>The ministry issued the following details:</p>
<p>						 Oct 96  Sep 96  Dec 95   Dec 94</p>
<p> External debt (million dollars)     1,636   1,646 1,312.6    771.8</p>
<p>Net Domestic debt (bln Lebanese</p>
<p>pounds)				    12,743  12,434 9,295.9  6,681.8</p>
<p>Total outstanding debt (million</p>
<p>dollars)				    9,826   9,624   n/a	n/a</p>
<p>The ministry did not issue figures for gross domestic debt.</p>
<p>($1 = 1,556 at end October)</p>
<p>- Beirut editorial (961 1) 864148 602057 353078</p>
</text>
